Z||000000||BJW||10-13-2000||02:30 AM||||So . . . my 87 5-speed V6 GT has these unusual problems. (or maybe they're not so unusual? - I had a 1985 V6 SE for 10 years and never  had these troubles!!!!)<BR>I CANNOT get the damn idle (when engine is warm) BELOW 1300 RPM . . . there are NO vacuum leaks, I have a new idle air valve, new CAT and  themostat (190degree) cause I thought that the temperature was staying too low for the idle to drop after the engine warmed up.<BR>Could it be the temperature sensor in the air cleaner? Or perhaps the fast idle extra fuel injector is stuck open?<BR>Also . . . at a stoplight, the idle takes at LEAST 15 seconds to drop to even the 1200 RPM! Why? . . . and then sometimes the CHECK ENGINE light comes on until I accelerate again. . . <P>Could it be the 100,000 miles on the 2.8?<P>The O2 sensor is OK, as far as I can tell (it checks out OK)<P>Or am I missing something?<P>Sure gets LOUSY fuel mileage with these problems!<P>B in Toronto||||reg||13
Z||000001||maninblack||10-13-2000||04:00 AM||||do you know what code you are getting?.I have the same year and model with 145000km.It<BR>had the same problem.at the time i didnt have a code reader so I was replacing my sensors one by one,until I replaced the MAP<BR>sensor the idle went back to "normal".Now it will hunt from 900 to 1000 at idle which is <BR>okay.||||reg||5
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-13-2000||08:08 PM||||Hope you get an answer to this one....Ive got an 87 GT with the exact same problem. It absoluty refuses to idle below 12-1300...everything on it has been changed to .....it also does that major 500-1500 idle surge for the first couple of minutes upon start up....driving me nuts! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||BJW||10-14-2000||02:03 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by maninblack:<BR>[B]do you know what code you are getting?<BR>- I am getting code 35 . . . the IAC (which I just replaced!)<BR>I know that if the idle speed is more than 50 RPM different from what the computer says it should be, it will lodge a 'code' . . . <BR>I wonder about the MAP sensor . . . as you say . . . that and/or the O2 sensor must be the problem . . . <BR>thanks for your help!<BR>B||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||10-14-2000||02:14 AM||||Well My idle is that high before it warms up... It was that high as well when my sensor for the cold start went screwy.  I thought the cold start injector would keep dumping excess fuel till the car warmed up.. Try disconnecting that injector...   if it runs fine then that is your problem...  (the cold start injector sensor looks just like the coolant temp one, but it is different internally if I am not mistaken...<P>BTW   the cold start injector on the v6 is by/underneath the distributor by the valley of the V...  it unplugs just like the normal injector wires but is a pain to get to!||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||10-15-2000||10:49 PM||||The cold start switch only works while the starter is engaged.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ka4nkf||10-15-2000||10:53 PM||||BTW the cold start switch on the V6 is next to the coolant fan switch by the thermostat housing.||||reg||1
